  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer planar dielectric filter stack with alternating Ta2O5 and SiO2 layers on Fused Silica substrate, air incident medium. Layer sequence: Ta2O5(1), SiO2(2), Ta2O5(3), SiO2(4), Ta2O5(5), SiO2(6), Ta2O5(7), SiO2(8), Ta2O5(9), SiO2(10), Ta2O5(11), SiO2(12), Ta2O5(13), SiO2(14), Ta2O5(15), SiO2(16), Ta2O5(17), SiO2(18), Ta2O5(19), SiO2(20). Seed thicknesses as follows: layers 1-12 start from base quarter-wave values (Ta2O5 ≈153 nm, SiO2 ≈263 nm) with linear chirp perturbation applied: layer 1 receives +0.5 nm offset, layer 12 receives -0.5 nm offset, with linear interpolation for layers 2-11. Layers 13-20 use base quarter-wave values (Ta2O5 ≈153 nm, SiO2 ≈263 nm, layer 20 ≈266 nm). Set optimization bounds to ±5.0 nm around each seeded thickness value. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Evaluate transmittance spectrum at normal incidence (0 degrees), unpolarized or both s and p polarizations. Score objectives: (1) mean transmittance at 1550 nm wavelength (single point), (2) mean transmittance across 1400-1500 nm band, (3) mean transmittance across 1600-1700 nm band. Target: maximize 1550 nm transmission, minimize both stopband transmissions. Total layer count fixed at 20. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a fixed 20-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 planar dielectric filter on fused silica to maximize transmittance at 1550 nm and minimize transmittance in 1400–1500 nm and 1600–1700 nm bands using gradient-based thickness optimization.",
